2026-11-26  Roman Senn  <roman.l.senn@gmail.com>

	* lib/key-events.js (reportKeys): New. Key status changes as events,
	seen at every availability load; lib/freellm.js, lib/availability.js use it.

	* lib/persist.js (appendEvent, readEvents), repl.js: quota, failover and
	proxy events are kept in events.jsonl (30 days).

	* lib/proxy-probe.js (torCookie, newnym, exitAfterNewnym, newExit),
	repl.js: cookie authentication for a local Tor, NEWNYM waits out
	newnym-wait, /proxy exit asks for the new address until it changes.

	* lib/exploration.js (Exploration#cost, costText), repl.js: /model health
	and the sweep event show the probes sent in 24 h and their tokens.

	* lib/probe-context.js (needlesFor, buildProbe), lib/exploration.js
	(probeUsable, run), repl.js (exploreOrder): the tier 1 probe takes a seed
	and varies its three facts per run, against prompt caching.

	* lib/exploration.js (Exploration#current, fresh, run): a passed entry
	of the old three-prompt code (no v 3) is asked once more from scratch.

	* TODO.md (A3): lists the files to delete as they are now (strace.log*,
	perf.data).

	* lib/context-view.js (messageText, messageSelection, summarizeMessages,
	parseContextArgs), repl.js (main): New. The pure parts of /context and
	/log moved out of repl.js, with tests.

	* lib/availability.js (loadAvailabilityNow, SLOW_TABLES): the chain and
	routing tables are asked once a minute, { fresh: true } asks all; the
	result has keyCounts.

	* lib/fallback-trail.js (spentPlatforms), repl.js (onMeta): when every key
	of a platform ran out in the trail, its models are skipped together.

	* lib/persist.js (usageRow, appendUsage), lib/usage-baseline.js (baseline),
	repl.js (watchNet): the explore, standby and sub-agent clients log their
	requests in usage.jsonl with a label; the baseline counts turns from the
	unlabelled (main) rows only.

	* repl.js (localCandidate): the local fallback client reports to the
	status line and /usage (onMeta).

	* lib/lag.js (timed, startLagWatch): New. Loop-lag watch and timed
	sections; slow rows in lag.jsonl carry the callers (where).

	* lib/run-command.js (runCommand): output goes to an unlinked scratch
	file, not a pipe, so a descendant holding the pipe cannot block the loop.

	* lib/availability.js (loadAvailability, groupId, limitsText): concurrent
	loads share one request set, { fresh: true } reloads after a change;
	groupId memoised; limitsText sorts on a flag worked out once per row.

	* lib/model-status.js (modelStatusTable): sort keys worked out once per row.

	* repl.js (allModelNames, /model skip): the names are copied, not
	filtered and sorted per model (a 4.8 s stall on a spent provider).

	* lib/provider-fallback.js (resetMs, classify): the cool-down of a limit
	follows Retry-After or "Soonest cooldown reset ~3m".

	* lib/transcript-text.js (earliestReset), repl.js: the give-up panel ends
	with the earliest reset time.

	* repl.js (flushState): ratings, quota snapshot and cooldowns are written
	on exit, /restart, SIGTERM and SIGHUP.

	* lib/hop-line.js (hopLine), repl.js (servedVia): a single-model hop names
	the provider that served the spent model.

	* lib/gateway-report.js (reportText): /gateway status explains the
	degraded mode without a dashboard session.

	* tests/test-turn-repair.js: a tool that throws mid round.
